{"chunk_id": "c-bca12f9ba03d2c84", "claim_id": "A031-c1", "containment_ok": true, "detail": "", "doc_id": "partials/storage-entry-size", "error_class": "", "item_id": "A031", "judge_reason": "", "judge_supported": null, "nli_score": null, "nli_supported": null, "quote": "For Vault deployments using the Consul storage backend, the default entry size limit is 512 KiB. The default size is enforced by Consul rather than Vault.", "span_end": 1084, "span_start": 930, "supported": true}
{"chunk_id": "c-bca12f9ba03d2c84", "claim_id": "A031-c2", "containment_ok": true, "detail": "", "doc_id": "partials/storage-entry-size", "error_class": "", "item_id": "A031", "judge_reason": "", "judge_supported": null, "nli_score": null, "nli_supported": null, "quote": "However, Consul **does not** chunk storage entries the way Vault does. Consul stores the entry as a single, large write.", "span_end": 1353, "span_start": 1233, "supported": true}
{"chunk_id": "c-bca12f9ba03d2c84", "claim_id": "A031-c3", "containment_ok": true, "detail": "", "doc_id": "partials/storage-entry-size", "error_class": "", "item_id": "A031", "judge_reason": "", "judge_supported": null, "nli_score": null, "nli_supported": null, "quote": "Even small changes may result in large read-modify-write cycles for storage entries, which can degrade Vault performance. Larger writes may also destabilize your Consul cluster by delaying heartbeats, which can lead to cluster leadership instability.", "span_end": 1604, "span_start": 1354, "supported": true}
{"chunk_id": "c-3c5a42ff9c3bbb23", "claim_id": "A032-c1", "containment_ok": true, "detail": "", "doc_id": "docs/internals/recommended-patterns", "error_class": "", "item_id": "A032", "judge_reason": "", "judge_supported": null, "nli_score": null, "nli_supported": null, "quote": "Since each token adds to the client count, and each unique authentication issues a token, you should use identity entities to create aliases that connect each login to a single identity.", "span_end": 2600, "span_start": 2414, "supported": true}
